# <%= @mod %>

A [Fractal](https://github.com/germsvel/fractal) application — an
AI-first web framework for Elixir. This app is a prompt-ready workspace:
the fundamental pattern is asking your AI agent to build it, and letting
`mix fractal.verify` prove the result correct.

## First run

```sh
mix deps.get        # if you haven't already
mix ecto.setup      # create the database
mix fractal.server  # http://localhost:4000, live reload on
mix fractal.verify  # the feedback loop — green from birth
```

## Quickstart: prompt, don't tutorial

Open your AI agent in this directory (it will find `AGENTS.md`) and ask:

- *Create a Fractal page at `/pricing` that lists three plans.*
- *Generate a `Post` resource with a title and a body, and list the
  latest posts on the home page.*
- *Add a nav bar with links to every page.* (The agent will create the
  app's layout module.)
- *Make the counter page count by tens.* (Then: *delete the counter
  page* — it's a demo.)
- *Add login with a session, and protect `/admin` behind it.*

After each change the agent runs `mix fractal.verify` — pages render,
routes are unique, styles are scoped, forms carry CSRF tokens, every
page has tests, and the app's invariants hold. If it's green, it works.

For smaller tweaks, use the **dev bar** in the browser: click "select
element" (bottom-right on any dev page), pick one devtools-style, type
what should change, and copy the composed prompt — it names the exact
files, so any agent lands on the right code without searching.

## Where things live

| Path | What |
| --- | --- |
| `lib/<%= @app %>/pages/` | One file per page — route, render, handlers together |
| `lib/<%= @app %>/components/` | Shared render-only UI components |
| `lib/<%= @app %>/checkpoints.ex` | Guards, expectations, and request context |
| `lib/<%= @app %>/invariants.ex` | House rules verify enforces on every page |
| `assets/app.css` | Design tokens and app-wide styles |
| `assets/static/` | Static files, referenced via `asset_path/1` |
| `test/<%= @app %>/` | The behavioral contract — verify fails untested pages |

## Docs

`mix fractal.ai.docs` prints the framework guides plus this app's live
inventories (components, guards, invariants). That's the same document
your agent reads before writing code.
